        },
        {
            "block_label": "algorithm",
            "block_content": "Algorithm 1: scContam audit pipeline\n\nInput: Benchmark B, reference subsample R, scFM θ, donor and cell-type metadata.\nOutput: Per-cell $\\{J^*(c), p_c\\}$; donor-matched gap statistics and permutation p.\n\n1 Step 1 (Signal A): Compute MinHash sketch ($m = 128$) for each $c \\in \\mathcal{B} \\cup \\mathcal{R}$;\n2 for $c \\in \\mathcal{B}$ do\n3 | Compute $J^*(c)$ via banded LSH ($b = 16$, $r = 8$) on $\\mathcal{R}$;\n4 | Draw 1000 permutation sketches; compute $p_c$ from Eq. 4;\n5 end\n6 Step 2 (Embedding): Extract $\\theta$-embedding $e_c$ for all $c \\in \\mathcal{B}$;\n7 Step 3 (Donor-matched gap):\n8 for each $(t, d)$ pair with $n_{\\text{clean}}, n_{\\text{contam}} \\geq n_{\\text{min}}$ do\n9 | Compute $\\Delta_{(t, d), \\theta}$ via Eq. 8;\n10 end\n11 Step 4 (Permutation null): Shuffle contamination labels within each $(t, d)$ group, repeat Step 3, $B = 500$ trials;\n12 Step 5 (Negative control, optional): Repeat Steps 3–4 on a Signal-A-clean dataset with random pseudo-contamination;",
            "block_bbox": [
